\chapter{Formatter, diagnostics, and repair proposals}
\label{ch:50}
\index{Formatter, diagnostics, and repair proposals}
\index{Diagnostics!scrutiny}
\index{Diagnostics!repair}

Use \OnxCodeTerm{on1xc fmt INPUT} for plain source output and \OnxCodeTerm{--check} for formatting checks. \OnxCodeTerm{--inplace} rewrites the source, and format targets include LaTeX or troff. The formatter uses \OnxCodeTerm{.on1xfmt} and avoids evaluating project scripts or PPX. It operates on source form, so successful formatting does not imply successful elaboration or backend lowering.

Compiler diagnostics have both a bounded catalog-backed path and legacy messages. The newer path supports policy such as \OnxCodeTerm{@scrutiny} and registered advisory delivery. In an eligible build, Wetstone supplies bounded static analysis and Syren emits supported JSON/SARIF output and repair proposals. A repair written to a separate path can be independently rechecked. Compare the edited source and run behavior tests even if the compiler accepts it. A range of unchecked or skipped HIR remains outside the advisory result. \cref{ch:89} follows the independent checkers.

